      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFor hybrid Mamba+attention architectures (e.g. NemotronH), `_init_estimated_perf_constants` in `metrics_reporter.py` scales both the attention-FLOPs term and the MLP-FLOPs term by `num_attention_layers`, which `ModelConfig` sets equal to `num_hidden_layers` for these models (no hybrid-Mamba special case exists there). In practice only a small fraction of layers are true attention layers; the rest are Mamba-mixer-only or MLP-only layers with no attention sublayer and, for Mamba layers, no MLP sublayer either.\n\nThis inflates the estimated prefill TFLOPS by roughly an order of magnitude for mostly-Mamba stacks. Concretely, on `nvidia/Nemotron-H-4B-Instruct-128K` (52 layers: 4 attention, 24 Mamba, 24 MLP-only), live on H200 (SGLANG_ENABLE_METRICS_DEVICE_TIMER=1, bench_serving, 1536-in/512-out, 500 prompts, concurrency 128), the device-timer-weighted ground-truth prefill TFLOPS was 1631.1 TFLOPS/s — 165% of H200's 989 TFLOPS/s physical peak, which is impossible. The same run after this fix reports 933.3 TFLOPS/s (94.4% of peak), a physically plausible value.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- In `_init_estimated_perf_constants`, read `hf_text_config.layers_block_type` (the per-layer type list the model builder itself reads at construction time, e.g. `models/nemotron_h.py`) when available, and derive separate `num_attn_layers` (count of `\"attention\"`) and `num_mlp_layers` (count of `\"mlp\"` + `\"moe\"`) instead of using a single shared `num_layers` for both.\n- Falls back to the existing `full_attention_layer_ids`-based attention-layer count (with `num_mlp_layers = num_layers`) when `layers_block_type` isn't present, preserving current behavior for non-hybrid architectures.\n- Scale `attn_linear_flops` by `num_attn_layers`, `mlp_flops` by `num_mlp_layers`, and `_attn_dot_flops_coeff` by `num_attn_layers` (previously all three were scaled by the same `num_layers`).\n- Mamba/SSM-layer compute itself is intentionally left uncosted (not estimated) rather than guessed at — a conservative gap that, if anything, slightly under-reports FLOPs/MFU for heavily-Mamba models rather than over-reporting.\n\nThis only affects the analytical FLOPs estimator used for `--enable-mfu-metrics` telemetry; it does not change model execution.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable — this only changes a telemetry estimator used for `est. prefill/decode TFLOPS/s` logging, not model forward computation.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nHardware-validated live on an H200 GPU running `nvidia/Nemotron-H-4B-Instruct-128K` with `SGLANG_ENABLE_METRICS_DEVICE_TIMER=1 --enable-metrics --enable-mfu-metrics`, using `sglang.bench_serving` (`--dataset-name random --random-input-len 1536 --random-output-len 512 --num-prompts 500 --max-concurrency 128`):\n\n| Stage | Ground-truth prefill TFLOPS/s | % of H200 peak (989 TFLOPS/s) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Before fix (all 52 layers costed as attention) | 1631.1 | 165% (impossible) |\n| After fix (4 attention, 24 MLP, 24 Mamba layers split correctly) | 933.3 | 94.4% |\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the Format code with pre-commit.\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the Run and add unit tests.\n- [ ] Update documentation according to Write documentations.\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to Test the accuracy and Benchmark the speed.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41778320311](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41778320311)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41778320143](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41778320143)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41778320123](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41778320123)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
